    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Kyle Tucker** (77.19), both of whom are clear starts against favorable matchups. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a high-upside combination of a +16% park factor and an 87% steal probability against a pitcher with a notably slow delivery, maximizing his elite speed metrics. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** is in a prime position to capitalize on a +19% SP skill boost against Bubba Chandler, making him our safest bet for high-leverage production. **Andy Pages** (72.73) rounds out our top tier; he remains an essential play today, leveraging that same +19% SP skill advantage and a high-value #3 lineup spot to provide reliable R/RBI production.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Dominic Smith**, who finished at 37.94, just shy of our strict 40-point efficiency floor. While he held a decent platoon edge, the matchup against a low-ERA arm like Misiorowski rendered him too risky to start, as we cannot afford to burn game caps on sub-floor projections. We are also keeping a close eye on the weather; both **Miguel Vargas** (49.17) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (41.50) face a 37% rain risk. While **Miguel Vargas** remains a justified start due to his high xwOBA and favorable #3 spot, **Luis Robert Jr.** is dangerously close to his floor. If the weather reports worsen, we may look to shuffle the utility slot. Meanwhile, our core remains bolstered by the continued absence of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, keeping the pressure on the active roster to maximize daily efficiency.",
